// SCOPE:core — Account-panel preferences: the palette list and the sound mute.
//
// Theme and sound are PREFERENCES, not navigation. A permanently visible
// icon toggle in the chrome is the wrong home for them: it competes with the
// identity row, and a two-state sun/moon control cannot express a catalog of
// four palettes (two of them dark) — switching from "Calmo" to dark silently
// threw the palette away. The research is one-sided: apps that moved the
// switcher out of the navbar did it into the account popover (PostHog #19001,
// Phoenix #14070, and the Vercel/Linear/Notion family keep preferences in
// account or settings), and platform guidance puts infrequent preferences in
// settings rather than in chrome (Material, Android, Windows). So: one place,
// the account panel, next to the identity that already tells you whose
// preferences they are.
//
// Rendered as <li> items because it composes into the account menu's list
// (authviews.UserMenu takes it as a slot, and the shell is its only host).
//
// The option is a toggle button carrying aria-pressed, not a single-select
// widget role: this list sits inside a disclosure of links, not inside a
// menu/listbox, and claiming those roles would promise arrow-key navigation
// this markup does not implement (it tabs, like the links around it). One
// pressed button out of four says the same thing to assistive tech and keeps
// the promise it makes.
//
// Attribute values here are scanned as styling candidates (see the exclusions
// in src/css/input.css), so a role or type named after a component library
// class would ship that component's CSS unused. Keep the vocabulary plain.
package ui

import (
	"github.com/calionauta/gogogo/internal/themes"
)

// Preferences renders the account panel's preference block: the palette list
// (one option per shipped theme) and, when the page passes one, the sound
// toggle it owns.
//
// Selection goes through the $theme SIGNAL (Datastar owns data-theme and the
// dark class through the bindings in authviews.ThemeRootAttrs) — writing the
// DOM directly is reverted. The names come from internal/themes, which
// themes_test.go keeps in step with the `themes:` list compiled by
// src/css/input.css.
templ Preferences(sound templ.Component) {
	<li class="app-pref">
		<p class="app-pref-head" id="app-pref-theme">Tema</p>
		<ul class="app-pref-list" aria-labelledby="app-pref-theme">
			for _, t := range themes.All {
				<li>
					<button
						type="button"
						class="app-pref-option"
						data-class={ "{'is-active': $theme === '" + t.Name + "'}" }
						data-attr:aria-pressed={ "($theme === '" + t.Name + "') ? 'true' : 'false'" }
						data-on:click={ "$theme = '" + t.Name + "'; localStorage.setItem('themeMode', $theme)" }>
						<span class="app-pref-swatch" data-theme={ t.Name } aria-hidden="true"></span>
						<span class="app-pref-label">{ t.Label }</span>
						<span class="app-pref-check" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					</button>
				</li>
			}
		</ul>
	</li>
	if sound != nil {
		<li class="app-pref-row">
			<label class="app-pref-setting">
				<span class="app-pref-label">Efeitos sonoros</span>
				@sound
			</label>
		</li>
	}
}
